          "content": {
            "size": 77972,
            "mimeType": "text/html",
            "text": "<div id=\"event-creator\" class=\"bantuan-section\" style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n  <h2 class=\"uk-text-center\">\n    <b>Event Creator</b>\n  </h2>\n  <p>\n    <span class=\"s1\"> Hello, welcome to <a href=\"http://www.loket.com\">\n        <span class=\"s2\">www.loket.com</span>\n      </a> website, managed and owned by PT Global Loket Sejahtera, the owner of LOKET ( <strong>\"Site\"</strong>). PT Global Loket Sejahtera is a limited liability company (LLC) engaged in the technology sector, specifically providing <em>software</em> in the form of a <em>platform</em> to facilitate and enhance the best user experience for enjoying <em>events</em> for you and <em>event creators</em> (hereafter referred to as <strong>\"LOKET\"</strong> or <strong>\"We\"</strong>). Any individual or legal entity using, accessing, utilizing, and/or creating an account on Our Site (hereafter referred to as <strong>\"You\"</strong>) is deemed to have understood, read, accepted, and agreed to the terms of use of the Site and LOKET services, as outlined below (hereafter referred to as <strong>\"Terms of Use\"</strong>). </span>\n  </p>\n  <p> These Terms of Use constitute a valid and binding agreement between You and LOKET. Please cancel your account and/or exit the Site and refrain from using, accessing, and/or utilizing this Site if you do not agree or do not wish to be bound by these Terms of Use. </p>\n  <p>\n    <b> PLEASE REVIEW LOKET'S TERMS OF USE AND PRIVACY POLICY CAREFULLY BEFORE USING THE SITE AND LOKET SERVICES FOR THE FIRST TIME. BY REGISTERING, CREATING AN ACCOUNT AND/OR USING THE SITE OR LOKET SERVICES, YOU PERSONALLY AND/OR THE LEGAL ENTITY YOU REPRESENT HAVE UNDERSTOOD AND AGREED TO BE BOUND BY AND COMPLY WITH ALL THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THESE TERMS OF USE AND LOKET'S PRIVACY POLICY. YOU HEREBY REPRESENT AND WARRANT TO LOKET THAT YOU ARE AN INDIVIDUAL OR A LEGAL ENTITY REPRESENTATIVE WHO IS LAWFULLY AUTHORIZED TO ACT AND BIND YOURSELF IN THIS AGREEMENT. </b>\n  </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> A. Definitions &amp; Interpretations </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> 1. Unless the context dictates otherwise, the following terms will have the meanings as defined below in these Terms of Use: </p>\n  <ol type=\"a\">\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong> \"LOKET\", \"we\", </strong>or <strong> \"us\"</strong> refers to PT Global Loket Sejahtera, a limited liability company established under Indonesian law and based in South Jakarta.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"You\"</strong> or \" <strong>User</strong>\" <strong></strong> refers to any individual or legal entity that uses, accesses, utilizes, and/or creates an account on <a href=\"http://www.loket.com\">www.loket.com</a>, including but not limited to Event Creators and Buyers.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Site\"</strong> means <a href=\"http://www.loket.com\">www.loket.com</a>, managed and owned by LOKET.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Platform\"</strong> means our Site, it's <em>mobile</em> version, voice and data channels, technology, software, systems, and other media owned and operated by LOKET from time to time.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Event\"</strong> refers to a commercial or non-commercial activity organized by an <em>Event Creator</em> who uses our Platform services to support the event's activities.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Event Creator\"</strong> refers to any individual, association, legal entity, and/or other legal bodies that organize an Event as organizers, promoters, committees, and/or owners collaborating with us using our Platform services, including but not limited to the services we provide on the Site.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Ticket\"</strong> means a valid proof of the right to enter the location of an Event, enjoy a performance presented by the Event, use and/or benefit from an activity related to the Event organized by the Event Creator according to the date, time, place, type, and/or other conditions attached to the ticket, which has been selected, booked, and purchased legally by the Buyer, in physical, electronic, or other media forms used by us from time to time, and is equipped with a unique code ( <em>barcode</em>) as a security system for the ticket.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Partner\"</strong> refers to parties that have entered into cooperation with us, including but not limited to cooperation in the reuse of our platform to provide Tickets both online and <em>offline</em> in person.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Buyer\"</strong> refers to any individual and/or legal entity who purchases, for a certain price or for free, Tickets organized by the Event Creator legally and in accordance with these Terms of Use, the terms and conditions applicable at the Event venue, the terms and conditions set by the Event Creator, and the applicable laws and regulations.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Loket.com\" </strong> refers to the service we provide for Event Creators in the form of a platform to support Events, offering convenience through the use of technology to help Event Creators create, market, sell, and/or distribute Events independently, with services that may change from time to time based on our policies.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"Service Fee\"</strong> refers to the fee for services provided by us in exchange for our services or products, including but not limited to providing the Platform to support your Event, whether in the form of money, percentages, or services that can be valued, as determined by us from time to time based on our policies.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>\n        <strong>\"E-Voucher\"</strong> or <strong>\"E-Ticket\"</strong> refers to an electronic ticket or voucher for an event such as a performance, concert, exhibition, festival, competition, seminar/conference.\n      </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> B. General Conditions </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> If there is a conflict or inconsistency between two or more provisions in these Terms of Use, whether with our other terms of use and/or the terms of use of our Partners, whether the provisions are listed in the same or different documents, then LOKET will determine which provisions shall apply. </li>\n    <li> In addition to these Terms of Use and depending on the services selected by You, You are required to read and accept the rules and terms of service that may apply to those services. </li>\n    <li> This agreement is effective for as long as You, the Event Creator, use our services, both during the event and after the event ends, until you have fulfilled all of your obligations under this agreement. </li>\n    <li> LOKET will publish any substantial changes or amendments to these Terms of Use (if any) through the Platform. The Event Creator is required to carefully read any changes or amendments, so that if the Event Creator continues to use, access, or utilize the Platform, the Event Creator is deemed to have acknowledged, understood, and agreed to those changes or amendments. </li>\n    <li> All Ticket orders by Buyers for Events organized by the Event Creator through our Platform constitute a separate obligation from the obligations arising from this agreement under these Terms of Use, namely an obligation between the Buyer and the Event Creator, each party being bound and subject to that obligation. To avoid doubt, we are the provider of the Platform working in cooperation with the Event Creator, while the entire Tickets sold to Buyers belong to the Event Creator. Any form of data and information regarding the Tickets provided by the Event Creator to us, and we communicate to potential Buyers, constitutes an offer from the Event Creator to those potential Buyers, which is binding upon the Event Creator and the Buyer in the case of a Ticket purchase. Therefore, we are not a party in the event of a dispute, claim for rights, legal action, claim for rights, demand for rights, indemnification, damages arising, injury, death, or any claim related directly or indirectly to the organization of the Event requested by the Event Creator to the Buyer, and vice versa, from the Buyer to the Event Creator, including by any third party who feels aggrieved by the Event organized by the Event Creator. </li>\n    <li> To avoid doubt, the Event Creator understands and agrees that LOKET does not provide any guarantees in any form regarding the success of the event, whether in terms of Ticket sales or the smooth execution of the Event. The Event Creator hereby releases and discharges LOKET and holds LOKET harmless from any claims, lawsuits, demands, damages, claims, and/or any form of compensation rights by any party, including the Event Creator themselves, arising from, including but not limited to, the results of Ticket sales and the organization of the Event. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> C. Event Creator Account </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> Each Event Creator wishing to use and utilize our services, including the Loket.com service, to support your Event, is required to create an account on the LOKET system. </li>\n    <li> The requirement to create an account is the provision of data and information by the Event Creator, whose truth, validity, legality, and authenticity are guaranteed by You. </li>\n    <li> Every action and conduct using the account is the full responsibility of the Event Creator as the creator and owner of the account, including any misuse by other parties and/or the Event Creator themselves. Therefore, the Event Creator is required to maintain the confidentiality of the data and information related to the account. The Event Creator releases and discharges LOKET from any responsibility in any form related to the use of that account. </li>\n    <li> In creating the account, all data and information filled in by the Event Creator are under the full control and ownership of the Event Creator, in which the Event Creator is fully responsible for the truth of each data and information filled in by the Event Creator, and any negligence, mistakes, errors, typos, and/or errors in any form and for any reason that cause the data and information to become meaningless as intended by the Event Creator, will be the full responsibility of the Event Creator, whether it causes loss or not, including but not limited to errors in bank account numbers, event schedules, event locations, and will be the responsibility of the Event Creator. <strong> Event Creator is required to fill in all information and data during the account creation process accurately, carefully, and with due diligence. </strong>\n    </li>\n    <li> You, as the Event Creator, hereby declare and guarantee to us that you are a legal entity with the right, a valid representative, authorized, the rightful owner, and/or have obtained all the necessary approvals in creating your account and filling in all data and information for your account creation. </li>\n    <li> You, as the Event Creator, hereby declare and guarantee to us that all data and information provided and filled in during the creation of your account is legal, valid, legitimate, and within Your authority to provide to us. </li>\n    <li> You hereby agree and consent that LOKET has the right to take necessary actions, including but not limited to deleting, not processing, blocking, or closing Your account, either temporarily (suspension of the User’s account) or permanently, and/or in any manner we deem necessary based on our policies, without prior notice to you in the event that the Event Creator’s activities are suspected or indicated to violate the Terms of Use, applicable laws, fraud, abuse, or theft (including indications of fraud, abuse, or theft), suspicious bookings, suspicion of criminal activity, providing inaccurate or misleading information, being difficult to contact, being listed on a \"blacklist\" by the government or international organizations. </li>\n    <li> By opening and using Your account on our Site, You release us from any responsibility, loss, and/or damages arising from the use of Your account, as well as if we take any actions we deem necessary in the enforcement of account provisions as outlined in point 7 above. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> D. Event Content </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> Event Creator who has created an account on our Site can create an Event subject to the terms and conditions in these Terms of Use, moral norms, public order, and applicable laws. </li>\n    <li> If applicable based on the service used, before the User begins ordering/purchasing an E-Ticket or E-Voucher, the User is directed to the waiting room page (hereinafter referred to as the \"LOKET Antrean\"). Regarding the LOKET Antrean, please refer to point E. </li>\n    <li> Event Creator is required to provide to us free of charge, without compensation in any form, all information and data regarding the Event, ensuring that the data and information are true, valid, legal, accurate, and do not violate the intellectual property rights of any other party in any form. The Event Creator is prohibited from creating a description of the Event that violates legal regulations, public order, morality, or applicable norms, such as but not limited to provocation against ethnicity, religion, race, and inter-group (SARA) issues, extortion, pornography, vulgarity, targeting certain individuals or groups, threats, insults, defamation, violence, intimidation, deception, lies, calls that stir hatred or hostility that divide, and/or calls to violate applicable laws. </li>\n    <li> The Event that the Event Creator organizes is prohibited from containing elements, whether in the form of naming, content of the Event, activities within the Event, location of the Event, and/or any form of elements related to and becoming an integrated part of the Event, either directly or indirectly, which include violations of legal regulations, money laundering, public order, morality, applicable norms, such as but not limited to gambling, prostitution, provocation against ethnicity, religion, race, and inter-group (SARA) issues, extortion, pornography, threats, insults, defamation, violence, intimidation, deception, lies, calls that stir hatred or hostility that divide, where the activities consist solely of money or goods collection without any other event activities, and/or calls to violate applicable laws. </li>\n    <li> Event Creator declares and guarantees to us that: <ol type=\"a\">\n        <li> All information and data provided to us, whether in the form of posters, images, words, terms, and/or other creations that are intellectual property rights, are the rights and authority of the Event Creator to use, either economically or non-commercially, for the benefit of the Event by the Event Creator. </li>\n        <li> The Event organized is the right, ownership, and full authority and/or represents the Event Creator’s authority to organize the Event, having received all necessary approvals. </li>\n        <li> The organization of the Event and its content, as well as the Event Creator’s compliance with this agreement, does not violate any provisions, whether based on legal regulations, other agreements, court orders, government orders, or any obligations the Event Creator is bound to comply with. </li>\n        <li> The Event Creator is fully responsible for the entire Event, including its content, side activities, or related elements, ensuring that it does not violate these Terms of Use, legal regulations, morality, public order, the intellectual property rights of others, and other regulations that must be adhered to. </li>\n        <li> The Event Creator has obtained all necessary permits, approvals, recommendations, and/or any other documents required for the implementation of the Event organized. </li>\n        <li> The content of the Event, whether the form of activities, participants in the activities, types of activities, event program, including types and classifications of Tickets and anything related to the Event's content created and filled in the LOKET system is true and in accordance with the actual situation. In case of any changes to the Event, including but not limited to location, type, time, activities, commercial to non-commercial nature or vice versa, ticket types and classifications, and other changes, the Event Creator is obligated to notify LOKET and/or Ticket Buyers about such changes. </li>\n      </ol>\n    </li>\n    <li> Event Creator hereby agrees to take full responsibility and release and discharge LOKET from all forms of liability, indemnity, claims, lawsuits, rights claims, and demands from any party and/or any obligations arising from violations of these Terms of Use, violations of legal regulations, violations of social norms, morality, public order, and/or violations of the rights of other parties affected by the execution of the Event and/or violations of prohibitions, declarations, guarantees, obligations, and all provisions of these Terms of Use. </li>\n    <li> Event Creator is fully responsible for obtaining all permits, approvals, exemptions, orders, licenses, taxes, levies, intellectual property usage approvals, and/or any documents required under legal regulations, including government policies, for the continuity and organization of the Event. </li>\n    <li> Event Creator hereby agrees and consents that LOKET has the full right and authority based on our policies to reject, delete, not process, blacklist, block, unilaterally terminate cooperation, claim damages, demand rights recovery, and/or take necessary actions as we see fit to handle any Event that we deem to have violated these Terms of Use, committed a criminal offense, violated legal regulations, public order, morality, fraud, abuse, negligence, carelessness, and/or based on policies we find justifiable. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> E. Queue/Waiting Room (\"LOKET Antrean\")</b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> The mechanism of LOKET Antrean is first come first served, in order to provide fair opportunities for Users. The order of ticket orders/purchases will be determined based on the arrival order of Users in the queue, and this is heavily influenced by the network and devices used by the Users. </li>\n    <li> The determination of User order is based on the data and information recorded in the LOKET system. LOKET will make reasonable efforts to ensure accuracy and provide equal service to each User, but LOKET is not responsible for technical errors, network failures, or transmission disruptions that may occur. </li>\n    <li> The queue number displayed on the LOKET Antrean page does not reflect the number of available tickets and cannot be used as a basis for ticket availability. LOKET does not guarantee the availability of tickets for all Users in the LOKET Antrean. Tickets may run out before a User reaches their turn for ordering/purchasing tickets. </li>\n    <li> When Users are on the LOKET Antrean page, they are advised not to perform any other activities on the device being used for ticket orders/purchases. Activities such as but not limited to opening other websites/apps, switching to another tab, refreshing the page, changing browser configurations, changing networks, using third-party apps/software (plug-ins/ads blockers, etc.), using a VPN, and so on. Users must pay attention to and understand these matters, as the system may remove Users from the queue page or transaction page if such activities occur. </li>\n    <li> Users, both Buyers and Event Creators, hereby agree and understand that they will be fully responsible and release LOKET from any liability, damages, claims, lawsuits, rights demands, and/or any form of obligations that may arise due to activities that cause Users to be removed from the LOKET Antrean page or transaction pages. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> F. Payment Terms </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> For each Event held by Event Creators on our Platform, we are entitled to Service Fees as stated at <a href=\"https://www.loket.com/panduan\"> https://www.loket.com/panduan </a> . </li>\n    <li> Before billing the proceeds from ticket sales through the LOKET system, the Event Creator must fill in and provide the necessary data and information as stated at <a href=\"https://www.loket.com/panduan\"> https://www.loket.com/panduan </a> . </li>\n    <li> Event Creator can bill for the proceeds from ticket sales through the LOKET system after the Event has ended and has met all applicable terms and conditions. </li>\n    <li> LOKET will process the payment for the invoice as referred to in paragraphs (2) and (3) above within a maximum of 10 (ten) working days from receiving and completing all the required information provided by the Event Creator. </li>\n    <li> Payments for the ticket sales proceeds will be made by LOKET via fund transfer to the Event Creator’s account based on the data and information filled by the Event Creator. Any mistakes in filling out the Event Creator’s account information causing delays, failures, losses, reductions, or any form of consequences arising from this will not be the responsibility of LOKET, and the Event Creator agrees and understands to release and exempt LOKET from liability for such issues. Therefore, the Event Creator must carefully, accurately, thoroughly, and cautiously provide the correct account details. </li>\n    <li> Event Creator guarantees and is fully responsible that the account information provided is a legitimate, valid, legal account owned by the Event Creator representing the Event. To avoid doubt, the Event Creator releases and exempts LOKET and will bear any claims, lawsuits, demands, orders, and claims from any party, including the Event Creator, regarding the proceeds from ticket sales sent to the account based on the information filled by the Event Creator. </li>\n    <li> Event Creator is fully responsible for all taxes, charges, contributions, levies, fees, interest, and/or invoices of any kind that are obligations related to the execution and organization of the Event. </li>\n    <li> Payments for ticket sales proceeds given to the Event Creator based on the sales report in the LOKET system will be paid after deducting our Service Fees, including value-added tax (VAT). </li>\n    <li> Unless otherwise specified in this agreement, all types of taxes, fees, or other levies, whether existing now or in the future, that must be paid to the government related to the transactions under this agreement, shall be borne by the Event Creator in accordance with applicable laws and regulations. </li>\n    <li> If the Event Creator does not make a claim for their rights, including ticket sales proceeds, within 30 calendar days from the end of the Event, the Event Creator hereby agrees to transfer those rights to us, and those rights shall become the exclusive property of LOKET. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> G. Event Changes and Cancellations </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> In the event of any changes to the Event activities caused by one reason or another, the Event Creator must notify us and the Buyer officially no later than 7 (seven) days before the change in the Event activities. </li>\n    <li> In the event of an Event cancellation, LOKET still has the right to retain the Service Fees that have been incurred and other costs that have been spent by the Second Party related to the implementation of the cooperation, including bank administrative fees for refund transfers to the Buyer and other related costs, which will be charged to the Event Creator. </li>\n    <li> In the event of an Event cancellation, the Event Creator is fully responsible for refunding the money from the Ticket purchases made by the Buyer through LOKET, by paying the fees as mentioned in Letter (G) point (2) above, plus the total refund amount for the Tickets, which will be deducted from the money received from the Ticket purchases, and the remaining amount must be paid by the Event Creator no later than 7 (seven) days through our account, which we will provide along with the amount to be paid to the Event Creator. </li>\n    <li> The refund amount for the Event cancellation to the Buyer is 100% (one hundred percent) of the Ticket price and does not include platform fees or other costs, which will be borne by the Event Creator, as stated in Letter (G) points (2) and (3) above. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> H. Lisencing </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> Subject to User's compliance with the Terms of Use, we grant User a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-assignable, non-sublicensable, revocable license to download and install a copy of the Site on a single mobile device that User owns or controls and to run the copy of the Site solely for User's own personal, non-commercial use. </li>\n    <li> User may not (i) copy, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works from, distribute, license, sell, assign, publicly display, reproduce, transmit, broadcast, reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble any portion of or otherwise exploit the Site, except as expressly permitted in these Terms of Use; (ii) license, sublicense, sell, resell, assign, transfer, distribute or commercially exploit or make available to any third party the Site and/or software by means of; (iii) create an Internet \"link\" to the Site or \"frame\" or \"mirror\" any software on any other server or wireless or Internet-based device; (iv) reverse engineer or access our software in order to (a) build a competing product or service, (b) build a product using the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, or (c) copy the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, (v) launch any automated program or script, including, but not limited to, web spiders, web crawlers, web robots, web ants, web indexers, bots, viruses or worms, or any program that may make multiple server requests per second, or otherwise unduly burden or hinder the operation and/or performance of the Site, (vi) use any robot, spider, site search/retrieval program, or other manual or automatic device or process to retrieve, index, \"data mine\" or in any way reproduce or circumvent the navigational structure or presentation of the Site or its contents; (vii) publish, distribute or reproduce in any way any copyrighted material, trademarks or other proprietary information without obtaining the prior consent of the owner of the proprietary rights, (viii) remove any copyright, trademark or other proprietary notices contained in the Site. No license or right is granted to Users by implication under any intellectual property rights owned or controlled by us or our licensors, except for the licenses and rights expressly granted in these Terms of Use. </li>\n    <li> Users shall not (i) copy, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works from, distribute, license, sell, assign, publicly display, reproduce, transmit, transfer, broadcast, decompile, or disassemble any part of or in any other way exploit the Site, except as expressly permitted in these Terms of Use; (ii) license, sublicense, sell, resell, assign, transfer, distribute or commercially exploit or make available to any third party the Site and/or software in any manner; (iii) create an internet \"link\" to the Site or \"frame\" or \"mirror\" any software on any other server or wireless or internet-based device; (iv) reverse engineer or access our software in order to (a) build a competing product or service, (b) build a product using the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, or (c) copy the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, (v) launch any automated program or script, including, but not limited to, web spiders, web crawlers, web robots, web ants, web indexers, bots, viruses or worms, or any program that may make multiple server requests per second, or otherwise unduly burden or hinder the operation and/or performance of the Site, (vi) use any robot, spider, site search/retrieval program, or other manual or automatic device or process to retrieve, index, \"data mine\" or in any way reproduce or circumvent the navigational structure or presentation of the Site or its contents; (vii) publish, distribute or reproduce in any way any copyrighted material, trademarks or other proprietary information without obtaining the prior consent of the owner of the proprietary rights, (viii) remove any copyright, trademark or other proprietary notices contained in the Site. No license or right is granted to User by implication under any intellectual property rights owned or controlled by us or our licensors, except for the licenses and rights expressly granted in these Terms of Use. </li>\n    <li> User shall not (i) copy, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works from, distribute, license, sell, assign, publicly display, reproduce, transmit, transfer, broadcast, reverse engineer, or disassemble any part of or in any other way exploit the Site, except as expressly permitted in these Terms of Use; (ii) license, sublicense, sell, resell, transfer, assign, distribute or otherwise commercially exploit or make available to any third party the Site and/or the software by any means; (iii) create an Internet \"link\" to the Site or \"frame\" or \"mirror\" any of the software on any other server or wireless or Internet-based device; (iv) reverse engineer or access our software in order to (a) build a competing product or service, (b) build a product using the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, or (c) copy the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, (v) launch any automated program or script, including, but not limited to, web spiders, web crawlers, web robots, web ants, web indexers, bots, viruses or worms, or any program that may make multiple server requests per second, or otherwise unduly burden or hinder the operation and/or performance of the Site, (vi) use any robot, spider, site search/retrieval program, or other manual or automatic device or process to retrieve, index, \"data mine\" or in any way reproduce or circumvent the navigational structure or presentation of the Site or its contents; (vii) publish, distribute or reproduce in any way any copyrighted material, trademarks or other proprietary information without obtaining the prior consent of the owner of the proprietary rights, (viii) remove any copyright, trademark or other proprietary notices contained in the Site. No license or right is granted to Users by implication under any intellectual property rights owned or controlled by us or our licensors, except for the licenses and rights expressly granted in these Terms of Use. </li>\n    <li> Users shall not (i) copy, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works from, distribute, license, sell, assign, publicly display, reproduce, transmit, transfer, broadcast, decompile, or disassemble any part of or in any other way exploit the Site, except as expressly permitted in these Terms of Use; (ii) license, sublicense, sell, resell, assign, transfer, distribute or commercially exploit or make available to any third party the Site and/or software in any manner; (iii) create an internet \"link\" to the Site or \"frame\" or \"mirror\" any software on any other server or wireless or internet-based device; (iv) reverse engineer or access our software in order to (a) build a competitive product or service, (b) build a product using the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, or (c) copy the Site's ideas, features, functions or graphics, (v) launch an automated program or script, including, but not limited to, web spiders, web crawlers, web robots, web ants, web indexers, bots, viruses or worms, or any program that may make multiple server requests per second, or otherwise unduly burden or hinder the operation and/or performance of the Site, (vi) use any robot, spider, site search/site retrieval program, or other manual or automatic device or process to retrieve, index, \"data mine\" or in any way reproduce or circumvent the navigational structure or presentation of the Site or its contents; (vii) publish, distribute or reproduce in any way any copyrighted material, trademarks or other proprietary information without obtaining the prior consent of the owner of the proprietary rights, (viii) remove any copyright, trademark or other proprietary notices contained in the Site. No license or right is granted to User by implication under any intellectual property rights owned or controlled by us or our licensors, except for the licenses and rights expressly granted in these Terms of Use. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> I. Intellectual Property Rights </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> We provide You with content such as audio, photos, images, videos, or other materials contained in sponsored advertisements or information. These materials may be protected by copyright, trademarks, or other intellectual property rights and laws. You may use these materials only as expressly permitted by LOKET and may not copy, transmit, or create derivative works of such materials without written permission from LOKET. </li>\n    <li> You acknowledge and agree that You will not download, post, reproduce, or distribute any content through the Platform that is protected by copyright or other proprietary rights of third parties without obtaining permission from the owner of such rights. Any exclusive copyright or other protected content distributed or through the Platform with the owner’s consent must contain the appropriate copyright or other ownership notices. Submission or distribution of unauthorized exclusive copyrighted content or other materials is illegal and may result in personal liability or criminal prosecution. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> J. MARKETING MATERIALS</b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> Event Creators grant their consent to LOKET and affiliates or parties working with LOKET to carry out promotional and/or marketing activities organized by Us, our affiliates, and/or parties working with us on LOKET Antrean and E-Voucher for Your Event. LOKET may place marketing and promotional materials on [LOKET Antrean], [E-Voucher], [E-Ticket], and/or any section that is part of the [Platform] of LOKET. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> K. Warranty </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> We do not make any statements, warranties, or guarantees about the reliability, timeliness, quality, suitability, availability, accuracy, or completeness of our services, our Site, and/or our Platform, including but not limited to Services obtained or derived from our Partners through the use of the Platform. We do not represent or warrant that (a) the use of the Platform will be secure, timely, uninterrupted, error-free, or operate in combination with other hardware, software, systems, or data, (b) the services will meet your needs or expectations, (c) any stored data will be accurate or reliable, (d) the quality of products, services, information, or other materials purchased or obtained by You through the Platform will meet your needs or expectations, (e) errors or defects in the Platform will be corrected, or (f) the Platform or the servers providing the Platform are free from viruses or other harmful components. Services are provided to You on an \"as-is\" basis. All conditions, representations, and warranties, whether express, implied, required by law, or otherwise, including but not limited to implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement of third-party rights, are hereby excluded and disclaimed to the fullest extent permitted by law. You acknowledge and agree that all risks arising from your use of the Platform are solely and entirely Yours, and You shall not have the right to seek any indemnity from us. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> L. Prohibited Use </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> As a condition for using the platform, You guarantee that You will not use this Platform for any purpose that violates current laws or is illegal under applicable laws in or outside of Indonesia, or prohibited by these terms and conditions and/or the Terms of Use, including both explicitly and/or implicitly. Furthermore, the Platform may not be used in any way that could damage, disable, overload, or disrupt the use of other parties and/or users of the Platform. You must comply and adhere to obtaining or attempting to obtain materials or information through means made available or provided through this Platform in good faith. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> M. Violations </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> Without prejudice to other rules available in these Terms of Use, our regulations, or under applicable law, we may restrict Your activities, warn Buyers or other parties regarding Your actions, lower and/or cancel Your Event, temporarily/permanently suspend or terminate Your registration and/or Event, including but not limited to Your account and/or Event, and/or deny access to the Platform, and/or take other actions based on our policy, if: <ol type=\"a\">\n        <li> You violate these Terms of Use, applicable laws, and/or other related documents; </li>\n        <li> The data and/or information You provide is unlawful, invalid, illegal, fraudulent, and/or unverifiable by us; or </li>\n        <li> We believe that Your actions may violate third-party rights or violate applicable law or result in liability for us, You, and/or other users, including potential Buyers. </li>\n      </ol>\n    </li>\n    <li> Subject to other provisions in these Terms of Use, in the event that Your Event is canceled by LOKET due to violation of any of these Terms of Use and/or applicable laws, any collected funds will be returned by LOKET to the Buyers. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> N. Limitation of Liability </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> We are not responsible for any injuries, deaths, damages, or losses that occur at the Event and/or use of the Platform. We are also not responsible for any errors, including violations, or criminal actions carried out by Buyers or other parties present at the Event location during the Event, including the Event Creator themselves. </li>\n    <li> We are not responsible, and You indemnify and hold us, our Partners, and our affiliates harmless from any losses, claims, lawsuits, and/or demands of any rights by You, Buyers, event attendees, and/or third parties for misuse, fraud, unfair practices and/or other actions resulting from the dissemination of information and/or Event data, including Event Ticket data, that You have personally made and/or due to Your negligence, oversight, and/or willful misconduct. Therefore, you are required to protect and not disseminate Your own personal information and data, including Your account. </li>\n    <li> Any claims against us in any matter by you will be limited to the total amount actually paid by and/or owed to You when using our services during the incident that led to the claim. Under no circumstances will we and/or our licensors be liable to yYouou or anyone for costs, interest, damages, or losses of any kind or form (including personal injury, emotional distress, and loss of data, property, revenue, profits, use, or other economic benefits). We will not be liable for any losses, damages, or injuries that may arise or be caused by You during the Event or in connection with the performance of this agreement or to any person for whom You have booked services, including but not limited to losses, damages, or injuries arising from, or in any way related to, services and/or the Platform, including but not limited to the use or inability to use the services and/or Platform and/or our Site. </li>\n    <li> You expressly waive and release us from any and all liabilities, claims, or damages arising from or in any way related to Buyers, Your partners, Partners, event attendees, parties present at the Event and/or the Event. We and our affiliates will not be parties to any disputes or negotiations of disputes between You and any party. The responsibility for the decisions You make regarding the Event lies entirely with You. You expressly waive and release us from any and all liabilities, claims, causes of action, or damages arising from the use of the Platform, the execution of the Event, the software and/or the Platform, or in any way related to us and our Partners introduced to You through the Platform. </li>\n    <li> We will take reasonable steps to prevent internet fraud and ensure that the data collected by us is stored securely. However, we are not responsible for any breaches on Your computer server; we are not liable as a third party. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> O. Indemnity </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> By using our services, You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold us, our licensors, affiliates, and each of our officers, directors, commissioners, employees, attorneys, and agents harmless from and against any and all claims, costs, damages, losses, liabilities, and expenses (including attorney’s fees) arising from or in connection with: (a) Your use of the services on our Site and/or Platform, Your relationship with Buyers, third-party providers, partners, advertisers, and/or sponsors; (b) A breach of or non-compliance with any of these Terms of Use or applicable laws, whether mentioned herein or not; (c) Your violation of the rights of third parties, including third-party partners and our Partners; or (d) The use or misuse of our Platform services. This indemnification obligation will remain in effect even if the Terms of Use and Your use of the Site and Event have ended. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> P. Other Conditions </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> If any provision in these Terms of Use is determined to be unlawful or unenforceable in whole or in part, defective, or must be interpreted only for that provision or part of the provision, the remaining part of that provision and all other provisions of these terms will continue to be in full force and effect, while that provision will be adjusted by us to make it enforceable and fully agreed upon by You. </li>\n    <li> These terms and conditions are governed by the laws of the Republic of Indonesia. </li>\n    <li> Any and all disputes arising from the use of this Site will be resolved through deliberation within 30 (thirty) calendar days. If the dispute cannot be resolved through deliberation after a notice of dispute, LOKET and the User agree to settle the dispute through the exclusive jurisdiction of the South Jakarta District Court, without prejudice to LOKET’s right to file a report, lawsuit, or claim, either civil or criminal, through the District Court, Police, or other relevant authorities within the territory of the Republic of Indonesia. </li>\n    <li> From time to time, we may unilaterally change, revise, amend, delete, add, and/or modify in any form the terms and conditions set out in these Terms of Use based on our policy and authority. </li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div id=\"buyer\" class=\"bantuan-section\" style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n  <h2 class=\"uk-text-center\">\n    <b>Buyer</b>\n  </h2>\n  <p>\n    <b> The following Terms &amp; Conditions constitute a binding agreement between PT Global Loket Sejahtera (\"LOKET\") and You (\"User\"). Therefore, the User MUST READ these Terms &amp; Conditions first. By using the LOKET.COM site, the User AGREES to COMPLY WITH and BE BOUND DIRECTLY by these Terms &amp; Conditions and Privacy Policy. </b>\n  </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> A. Use of The Loket.Com Site</b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> The LOKET.COM site (\"Site\") and the services available within it can only be used by Users for personal purposes, specifically for booking and/or payment purposes. </li>\n    <li> The Terms and Conditions are integral to the Privacy Policy. Users agree to abide by these Terms and Conditions and the Privacy Policy as outlined on this page. </li>\n    <li> This Site and the products, technologies, and processes contained within it are owned by LOKET and/or third parties who grant rights to LOKET. Except for uses expressly permitted and allowed under these Terms and Conditions, Users neither own nor receive, and LOKET does not grant any other rights over this Site, including all data, information, and content within it. </li>\n    <li> By using this Site or the services available on it, the User agrees not to: <ol type=\"a\">\n        <li>\n          <p> Use the Site for any purpose other than those explicitly stated. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Access, monitor, or copy any content or information from the Site using robots, spiders, scrapers, or any automated or manual processes for any purpose without LOKET's prior written consent. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Violate any restrictions in the Site's robots exclusion headers or bypass or circumvent other measures implemented to prevent or limit access to the Site. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Take any action that imposes, or could impose, in LOKET’s opinion, an unreasonable or disproportionately large load on LOKET's infrastructure. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Deep-link to any part of the Site (including, but not limited to, purchase paths) for any purpose without LOKET’s prior written consent. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Resell, use, monitor (e.g., spider, scrape), display, download, or reproduce any content, software, products, or services available on the Site for any commercial or competitive activities or purposes. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Frame, mirror, or otherwise incorporate any part of the Site into any other site without LOKET’s prior written consent. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Send unlawful messages (according to applicable regulations) to or through the Site, or messages reflecting illegal activities. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Transmit or provide links to messages containing materials that are harmful, immoral, pornographic, inappropriate, offensive, violent, abusive, indecent, racist, discriminatory, defamatory, threatening, harassing, or hateful. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Transmit or provide links to messages containing defamatory materials that harm individuals or entities. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Transmit any message that infringes or violates the intellectual property rights or other rights of any entity or person, including but not limited to copyrights, patents, trademarks, trade secrets, or rights of privacy or publicity. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Transmit any message without legal rights under applicable law. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Impersonate any person or entity or falsely state, or misrepresent, your affiliation with a person or entity, or use false identities to mislead, deceive, or defraud others. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Engage in manipulation, such as falsifying headers, to disguise the origin of messages sent by the User. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Use the Site in any way that damages, disables, overburdens, or impairs it or interferes with other users’ access to or use of the Site or their computer equipment, or that causes damage, disruption, or limits the functionality of any software, hardware, or telecommunications equipment. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Attempt unauthorized access to the Site, related sites, other accounts, computer systems, or networks connected to the Site through hacking, password theft, or other means. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Obtain or attempt to obtain materials or information through means not intentionally provided through the Site, including gathering or collecting information about others, such as email addresses. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Engage in fraudulent practices aimed at manipulating organic Search Engine Results Pages (SERP) or using Search Engine Optimization (SEO) techniques considered inconsistent with prevailing search engine guidelines. These include, but are not limited to, cloaking, metadata/title tag manipulation, content scraping, link schemes, Google bombs, keyword stuffing, hidden text and links, doorway and cloaked pages, link farming or schemes, blog comment spam, etc. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Engage in any actions that could harm the Site, LOKET’s group companies, directors, employees, reputation, or cause any other negative impacts. </p>\n        </li>\n      </ol>\n    </li>\n    <li> The Site may contain links to websites managed by third parties (\"External Sites\"). External Sites are provided solely for reference and convenience. LOKET does not operate, control, or endorse External Sites or their content in any form. Users are fully responsible for using External Sites and must carefully review the terms and conditions of such External Sites. </li>\n    <li> The services available on this Site generally use remarketing and cookie systems, enabling third parties (including but not limited to Google and Yahoo) to access and use visit data within the Site’s cookie system to display and re-present LOKET advertisements via the internet. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> B. LOKET SERVICES </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> LOKET provides and organizes systems and facilities for booking tickets or vouchers in the form of electronic tickets (\"E-Tickets\") or electronic vouchers (\"E-Vouchers\") for a performance, concert, exhibition, festival, match, seminar/conference (\"Event\"), as well as making purchases and at the same time making payments online and securely through various payment systems and facilities available. </li>\n    <li> LOKET services are generally available online twenty-four hours a day and seven days a week; except in the event of repairs, upgrades or maintenance on the Site. </li>\n    <li> Events are organized by third parties (\"Partners\") who have entered into cooperation and have entered into a binding agreement, either directly or indirectly, with LOKET. </li>\n    <li> Users understand and acknowledge that: <ol>\n        <li>\n          <p> The order/purchase that the User makes through LOKET, constitutes a binding legal and contractual relationship between the User and the Partner. In this case, LOKET acts as an intermediary whose task is to facilitate transactions between Users and Partners. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> The data and information related to the Event that LOKET lists on the Site are data and information that LOKET receives from the Partner, and LOKET will publish the data and information in good faith in accordance with the data and information that LOKET receives. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> LOKET has no control over the data and information provided by Partners, and LOKET does not guarantee that the data and information presented are accurate, complete, or correct, and free from errors. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Users are not allowed to resell E-Tickets or E-Vouchers, use, copy, monitor, display, download, or reproduce any content or information, software, or Services available on the Site for any commercial activities or purposes, without prior written approval from LOKET. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> Users may only use the Site and available Services to make legitimate bookings/purchases. Users are not allowed to make bookings/purchases for speculative, improper or unlawful purposes. If LOKET finds or reasonably suspects that the booking/purchase made by the User is not legitimate, then LOKET has the right to cancel the E-Ticket or E-Voucher booking/purchase. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> User also guarantees that the data and information that the User provides to LOKET, both in connection with ordering/purchasing on LOKET, is accurate, current, and complete data and information. </p>\n        </li>\n        <li>\n          <p> The User agrees and understands that LOKET is not responsible for all and any data and information provided by the Event Organizing Partner, along with all changes (if any). The User releases LOKET from all forms of claims for this matter. </p>\n        </li>\n      </ol>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> C. RESERVATION/PURCHASE &amp; PAYMENT </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> Users can order/purchase E-Tickets or E-Vouchers available through the official LOKET website. Under any circumstances, LOKET is not responsible for ordering/purchasing E-Tickets or E-Vouchers made through other sites that are not the official LOKET website. For this reason, Users must carefully check the address of LOKET's official website when making an order/purchase. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Before the User starts ordering/purchasing E-Tickets or E-Vouchers, the User is directed to the queue page/ waiting room (hereinafter referred to as \"LOKET Queue\"). Regarding LOKET Queue refer to point D. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Event organizing partners may apply E-Tickets or E-Vouchers in various categories or classes, dates and hours of the Event, as well as apply the type of E-Ticket or E-Voucher for one-time entry to the Event venue (single entry) or multiple entries to the Event venue (multiple entry). Therefore, before placing an order/purchasing an E-Ticket or E-Voucher, the User must pay attention to the category or class, date and time of the Event as well as the type of E-Ticket or E-Voucher that the User desires. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> In the event that the User makes an order/purchase of an E-Voucher, then in order to enter the venue of the Event, the User must redeem the E-Voucher with a ticket or ticket with barcode or wristband with barcode or wristband with Radio Frequency Identification (RFID) as applicable, at the time and place determined by the Event organizing Partner. LOKET requires the User to redeem the E-Voucher itself with tickets or tickets with barcodes or wristbands with barcodes or wristbands with Radio Frequency Identification (RFID). If the User requests a third party to redeem the E-Voucher, the User hereby takes full responsibility and therefore releases and protects Loket from all forms of claims if the third party fails or neglects or does not submit tickets or tickets with barcodes or wristbands with barcodes or wristbands with Radio Frequency Identification (RFID) to the User. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> To make an order/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers, the User must fill in personal data in accordance with the data stated on the User's identity card (Identity Card/Driver's License/Passport) which is valid and still valid. LOKET and/or the Event organizing Partner has the right to cancel the booking/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers at any time if it is known that the User is using incorrect data or a fake identity card or one that has expired. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> For Performances/Events that are marked with a minimum age (e.g. 17+, 18+, 21+), ticket users who are less than the minimum age stated are not allowed to enter the performance area for any reason. There will be no refund or compensation in any form. Age validation can only be done by showing the user's original valid identity card. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> E-Ticket or E-Voucher booking/purchase is considered successful or completed after LOKET receives confirmation of successful payment of E-Ticket or E-Voucher booking/purchase in the LOKET system, and LOKET will issue and send an e-mail confirmation of E-Ticket or E-Voucher booking/purchase to the User's e-mail address. To avoid doubts, LOKET will send a confirmation e-mail to the User's e-mail address through the account support@loket.com. A confirmation e-mail sent other than from the account is not a confirmation e-mail issued and sent by LOKET and becomes valid and binding evidence that the User did not make an order/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers through the official LOKET website. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The User hereby acknowledges that payment transaction failures can occur at any time due to banking system failures, and the User hereby agrees that in the event of a banking system failure, the booking/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers is considered unsuccessful. In the event of a dispute in the future in connection with the booking/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers, the User hereby agrees that the data contained in the LOKET system is the only valid evidence and binds LOKET and the User. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Users can make payments using credit cards, inter-account and inter-bank transfers or virtual accounts at the banks listed on the Site or other payment methods. To protect the User's credit card information, LOKET uses encryption technology facilities; however, LOKET does not provide any guarantee regarding the effectiveness of encryption technology, and the User hereby agrees that LOKET is not responsible for problems that occur due to unauthorized access of the information that the User provides. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> In the event of a case of credit card fraud or misuse of the payment system by any third party, the incident must be immediately reported to LOKET and the User's credit card issuing bank within 1x24 hours. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> For the payment of E-Ticket or E-Voucher bookings/purchases through a transfer mechanism between accounts or virtual accounts, the User is required to make payment payments no later than 3 (three) hours from the time the E-Ticket or E-Voucher booking/purchase is made. LOKET reserves the right to cancel the booking/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers made by the User, if LOKET has not received confirmation of successful payment in the LOKET system at the specified time. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Subject to the provisions of point C.9 above, in the event that the Partner applies a \"Pre-Sale\" or \"Early Bird\" sales system, the User is required to make payment settlements on the same day when the User places an order/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers. If the User, for any reason or cause, fails to make a payment settlement transaction at the specified time, then LOKET has the right to cancel the order/purchase made by the User, and the User can make an order/purchase again as long as the Pre-Sale or Early Bird E-Ticket or E-Voucher is still available. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> By completing a reservation/purchase, users agree: </p>\n    </li>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>\n        <p> To receive e-mails that LOKET will send immediately after the User completes the booking/purchase of an E-Ticket or E-Voucher, providing the User with information about the E-Ticket or E-Voucher that the User ordered/purchased, and providing the User with certain information and offers (including third party offers that the User selects) related to the User's booking/purchase. </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <p> To receive e-mails that LOKET will send to invite Users to complete the user review form of LOKET services. In addition to e-mails regarding confirmation of booking/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers and e-mails of third-party offers that the User has chosen themselves, LOKET will not send the User notifications (desired or not), e-mails, further correspondence, unless specifically requested by the User. </p>\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> E-Tickets or E-Vouchers that have been ordered/purchased and paid for by the User, cannot be canceled or returned or cashed or resold, or transferred in any way to others for any reason. The User hereby agrees to compensate for all losses suffered by LOKET and to release and protect LOKET from all forms of claims filed by any party arising in connection with the resale or transfer of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers by the User to others. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> In the event that the Event is cancelled by the Event organizing Partner, the User hereby agrees that the policy of refunding the purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers is fully under the authority of the Event organizing Partner, and the User hereby agrees not to submit claims in any form to LOKET in connection with the cancellation of the Event and refunding the purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers. Bank fees and administrative fees that have been charged to the User when ordering/purchasing E-Tickets or E-Vouchers, will not be refunded. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The refund provisions will follow the provisions as regulated by the Event organizing Partner which will be conveyed by LOKET to the User in accordance with the conditions of the Event. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The User agrees that ticket refunds made not through LOKET are not the responsibility of LOKET. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> In the event of a ticket refund, the refunded value is according to the ticket price paid by the User. In the event that the User uses a unique code, voucher, discount code, promo code and/or other reductions as provided by LOKET and/or other parties, the reduction will not be returned to the User. LOKET will return to the issuer of the reduction or according to LOKET's provisions. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The User hereby releases LOKET from all forms of claims in the event of a ticket refund. </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> D. Queue/Waiting Room (\"LOKET Antrean\") </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li> The mechanism of LOKET Antrean is first come first served, in order to provide fair opportunities for Users. The order of ticket orders/purchases will be determined based on the arrival order of Users in the queue, and this is heavily influenced by the network and devices used by the Users. </li>\n    <li> The determination of User order is based on the data and information recorded in the LOKET system. LOKET will make reasonable efforts to ensure accuracy and provide equal service to each User, but LOKET is not responsible for technical errors, network failures, or transmission disruptions that may occur. </li>\n    <li> The queue number displayed on the LOKET Antrean page does not reflect the number of available tickets and cannot be used as a basis for ticket availability. LOKET does not guarantee the availability of tickets for all Users in the LOKET Antrean. Tickets may run out before a User reaches their turn for ordering/purchasing tickets. </li>\n    <li> When Users are on the LOKET Antrean page, they are advised not to perform any other activities on the device being used for ticket orders/purchases. Activities such as but not limited to opening other websites/apps, switching to another tab, refreshing the page, changing browser configurations, changing networks, using third-party apps/software (plug-ins/ads blockers, etc.), using a VPN, and so on. Users must pay attention to and understand these matters, as the system may remove Users from the queue page or transaction page if such activities occur. </li>\n    <li> Users, both Buyers and Event Creators, hereby agree and understand that they will be fully responsible and release LOKET from any liability, damages, claims, lawsuits, rights demands, and/or any form of obligations that may arise due to activities that cause Users to be removed from the LOKET Antrean page or transaction pages. </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> E. PRICE </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> The prices displayed on the Site do not include platform fees, as stated in the confirmation email or other electronic confirmation. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> F. USE OF E-TICKET OR E-VOUCHER &amp; TERMS FOR ENTERING THE EVENT VENUE </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> User hereby acknowledges and agrees that: </p>\n  <ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET will only send E-Tickets or E-Vouchers through the official LOKET account, namely to the e-mail address and/or other media owned by the User submitted by the User to LOKET when the booking/purchase is made. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET will only send the E-Ticket or E-Voucher after the booking/purchase transaction is considered successful or completed and LOKET has received confirmation of successful payment of E-Ticket or E-Voucher booking/purchase in the LOKET system. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> To avoid duplication or misuse of E-Tickets and E-Vouchers, only the User can access the User's e-mail and the User will only print the E-Ticket or E-Voucher 1 (one) time for the User's own use. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> 1 (one) E-Ticket or E-Voucher is only valid for 1 (one) person and 1 (one) use, in accordance with the category or class, date and time of the Event arranged by the Event organizing Partner. The Event organizing Partner has the right to refuse the User to enter the venue of the Event that is not in accordance with the E-Ticket or E-Voucher ordered/purchased by the User. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The User is obliged to maintain confidentiality and is prohibited from publishing E-Tickets or E-Vouchers that have been ordered/purchased, including publishing through social media, to avoid duplication/multiplication or use of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers or barcodes printed on E-Tickets or E-Vouchers by third parties. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET and/or the Event Creator partner under any circumstances is not responsible if the E-Ticket or E-Voucher or the barcode printed on the E-Ticket or E-Voucher is printed more than 1 (one) time or duplicated/duplicated by a third party or falls into the hands of a third party or is in the possession of a third party to then be used by the third party to enter the event venue. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The user must show a valid and still valid identity card (Identity Card/Driver's License/Passport), which is used by the User to place an order/purchase E-Ticket or E-Voucher. The Event Creator has the right to refuse the User to enter the venue of the event if the user fails to show his/her identity card. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> In the event that the payment of an E-Ticket or E-Voucher is made using a credit card, the User must bring and show the physical of the credit card used to make the booking/purchase to the Event Creator to enter the venue of the event. The Event Creator has the right to refuse the User to enter the venue of the event if the user fails to show the credit card. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The Event Creator reserves the right to refuse Users who are under 18 years old and/or who do not have an identity card, who are not accompanied by at least 1 (one) adult, to enter the event venue. Furthermore, LOKET and/or the Event Creator is not obliged to make a refund to the user. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> If the Event is sponsored by a cigarette company and/or alcoholic beverage company and/or contraceptive company, then the Event Creator has the right to refuse Users who are under 18 years old to enter the event venue. Furthermore, LOKET and/or the Event Creator is not obliged to make a refund to the User. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The Event Creator reserves the right to refuse the user to enter the event venue in the event that the user is deemed to have the potential to disrupt the security and comfort of the event, is intoxicated, under the influence of drugs, carrying/possessing narcotics and illegal drugs, carrying sharp weapons (or the equivalent thereof), carrying firearms (or the equivalent thereof). In such case, the Event Creator has the right to report and hand over the user to the authorities. Furthermore, LOKET and/or the Event Creator is not obliged to make a refund to the user. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Users are prohibited from bringing food and/or beverages from outside the event venue. The Event Creator reserves the right to confiscate food and/or beverages from outside the event venue brought by the User. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The Event Creator reserves the right to refuse the User to enter the event venue or remove the user from the event venue if the user behaves in a disorderly manner, incites disputes, or refuses instructions/warnings from the Event Creator staff. Furthermore, LOKET and/or the Event Creator are not obliged to make a refund to the user. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> User is obliged to take care of his/her personal belongings during the event. LOKET and/or its Event Creator shall under no circumstances be liable for any loss suffered by the user. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> User hereby releases LOKET and/or Event Creator from all forms of claims in the event of cancellation of the event which is carried out unilaterally by the artist or government or for other reasons beyond the ability and will of LOKET and/or Event Creator. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> User hereby releases LOKET from all forms of claims in the event of cancellation of the event and/or postponement of the event. </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> G. LIABILITY </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> The entire contents of the Site, including but not limited to software, information, materials, text and graphics are provided to the User as is. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET makes no representations or warranties of any kind, either implied or expressed, with respect to the operation or information or materials or text or graphics of this Site. LOKET also makes no representations or warranties of any kind, either implied or express, that the information or materials or text or graphics of this Site are free from infringement of third party rights. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET makes no representations or warranties of any kind, either implied or express, that the Site will operate without error or interruption, that any defects will be corrected, that the Site and/or its servers are free of viruses and/or other harmful components. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET makes no representations or warranties of any kind, either implied or expressed, as to the suitability, availability, accuracy, reliability, completeness, timeliness of the entire operation or information or material or text or graphics of this Site. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET is not responsible for any failures caused by server errors, misdirected or redirected transmissions, internet connection failures, transmission interruptions, reception failures, viruses or other defects, whether of a human error or technical error nature. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> To the fullest extent permitted by law, under no circumstances will LOKET (including its directors, commissioners, officers, employees, representatives, affiliates, distributors, suppliers, licensors, agents, or any other party involved in creating, sponsoring, promoting or otherwise making available the Site and its contents (\"Indemnified Parties\"), be liable to any person or entity for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, general, consequential or punitive damages or any loss or damage of any kind, including but not limited to loss of production, loss of profits, loss of revenue, loss of contracts, loss of reputation, loss of claims, business interruption, loss or corruption or interruption of data, other intangible losses, User's inability to use the Site, unauthorized access to User's personal information, errors or inaccuracies of material or information or text or graphics on the Site, any property damage, including damage to User's computer caused by viruses or other harmful components, during or due to accessing or using this Site. This limitation of liability applies regardless of the form of action, whether based on contract, tort, negligence, liability, or other matters. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> In the event of force majeure, the Indemnified Party is released from all obligations under these Terms and Conditions. Force majeure is an event that occurs beyond the control of the Indemnified Party, and may include, but is not limited to, natural disasters, weather conditions, fires, nuclear incidents, electromagnetic vibrations, terrorist acts, riots, wars, attacks causing fire, riots, insurrections, armed violence in any form, labor disputes, lock-outs, strikes, shortages, government actions or prohibitions, theft, bankruptcy, breakdown of machinery, disconnection or interruption of networks or systems, disconnection of internet and communication connections, quarantine, epidemics, pandemics, and others. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> To the extent permitted by law, LOKET is only responsible for losses directly suffered by Users, as a result of LOKET's direct fault. Under any circumstances, LOKET's liability is only limited to the total amount of payment that has been paid by the User in accordance with the details stated in the booking/purchase confirmation e-mail. </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> H. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> LOKET owns the copyright to the Site. Users may not use the intellectual property rights of LOKET without LOKET's consent. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Product and company names mentioned in the Site may be names, trademarks, trade names, service marks, logos, symbols or other proprietary things of LOKET, its licensors, or associated companies or third parties. The use in the Site of any names, trade names, trademarks, service marks, logos, symbols or other proprietary marks or markings of or belonging to third parties, shall not be construed as an endorsement or sponsorship by LOKET, or the participation of such third parties in the Site. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> The Site contains copyrighted materials, trade names and other proprietary information, including, but not limited to text, software, photographs, graphics, video, music and sound. The entire content of the Site is protected by copyright law. Users are not entitled to modify, create, transmit, transfer, sell, create derivative works, or in any way exploit, any content of the Site, whether in whole or in part. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Unless otherwise stated, the software required for Our services or available on, or used by the Site and the intellectual property rights (including trademarks, service marks, logos, designs, copyrights, etc.) to the content and information and materials on the Site are owned by LOKET, its affiliates, its licensors, its suppliers. LOKET is not responsible for any copyrighted material provided by third parties or any infringement of intellectual property rights by such third parties. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Unless otherwise expressly provided under copyright law, User is prohibited from duplicating, redistributing, retransmitting, publishing or commercially exploiting any material that User has downloaded in any form, without written permission from LOKET. </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> I. MARKETING MATERIALS </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> The User gives consent to LOKET and its affiliates or parties working with LOKET to be able to send the User direct marketing, advertising and promotional communications via push-notification applications, messages or placements via Loket.com, post, telephone calls, short message service (SMS), E-Vouchers, in LOKET Live shows or streaming media, and email (\"Marketing Materials\"). Users may opt-out of receiving such marketing communications at any time by clicking on the \"unsubscribe\" option contained in the relevant message, other methods as provided or contacting Loket via the contact details listed below. Please note that if User opts out, We may still send User non-promotional messages, such as receipts or information about User Account. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> J. DISPUTE RESOLUTION </b>\n  </h3>\n  <p> Any disputes arising between Loket and User in connection with the use of the Site and/or the booking/purchase of E-Tickets or E-Vouchers, will first be resolved by deliberation to reach consensus. If the dispute cannot be resolved within 30 (thirty) calendar days after the dispute notification letter, then LOKET and User agree to resolve the dispute through the South Jakarta District Court in Jakarta. </p>\n  <h3>\n    <b> K. MISCELLANEOUS </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> These Terms and Conditions are made in the Indonesian language. Any translation into other languages is for convenience only and does not constitute an official translation. In the event of any discrepancy between the Indonesian version and any other language, the Indonesian version shall prevail. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p>These Terms and Conditions are subject to the laws of the Republic of Indonesia.</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> If there are certain parts in these Terms and Conditions which for any reason are deemed invalid or invalid, then the other parts of these Terms and Conditions remain valid and binding. </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> We may change, modify, add, delete or correct these Terms of Use (\"changes\") from time to time. We will use reasonable efforts and timeframes to notify You of any material changes to these Terms of Use electronically where You may choose to continue using the Site or refuse to comply by discontinuing use of the Site immediately. However, you understand and agree that it is your responsibility to review these Terms of Use periodically and your continued use of the Site constitutes your acceptance of any changes to the Site Terms of Use. </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n  <h3>\n    <b> L. HELP CENTER </b>\n  </h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li>\n      <p> The best way to contact us is by email at <a href=\"mailto:cs@loket.com\">support@loket.com</a>. The phone number you can reach is +6221 30003160. <br>\n      </p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <p> Customer Service <br>\n        <b>DIRECTORATE GENERAL OF CONSUMER PROTECTION AND TRADE ORDER MINISTRY OF TRADE OF THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA</b>\n        <br>\n      </p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n</div>"
          },
