          "content": {
            "size": 31695,
            "mimeType": "text/html",
            "text": "<ul class=\"event-content uk-switcher uk-margin\" style=\"touch-action: pan-y pinch-zoom; list-stype: none; padding: 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify\">\n  <li class=\"uk-active\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Definition</b>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"tnc uk-text-justify\">The following Privacy Policy explains how We, (PT Global Loket Sejahtera, Our affiliates, and parties who work with Us specifically to provide services, products and/or services to You, hereafter referred to as \" <b>We</b>\") collect, store, use, process, control, transfer, disclose and protect Your Personal Information. This Privacy Policy applies to every customer and/or user (\" <b>Customer</b>\") and ticket provider as the ticket owner and/or ticket provider (\" <b>Ticket Provider</b>\") on the Loket site ( <a href=\"https://www.loket.com\" class=\"ss-link-text\">https://www.loket.com</a>) (\" <b>Platform</b>\"), unless regulated in a separate privacy policy. </p>\n    <p class=\"tnc uk-text-justify\">Please read this Privacy Policy carefully to ensure that you understand how we collect, use and process your data. Unless otherwise defined, all capitalized terms used in this Privacy Policy have the same meaning as stated in the Platform Terms of Use.</p>This Privacy Policy covers the following: <ol>\n      <li>Definition</li>\n      <li>Collection of Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Use of Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Disclosure of Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Retention of Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Access and Correction of Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Where We Store Your Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Security of Personal Information</li>\n      <li>Changes to the Privacy Policy</li>\n      <li>Acknowledgement and Consent</li>\n      <li>Marketing and Promotional Materials</li>\n      <li>Anonymous Data</li>\n      <li>Third Party Platforms</li>\n      <li>How to Contact Us</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Collection of Personal Information</b>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"tnc\">We collect information that identifies or can be used to identify, contact, or locate the person or device to whom such information pertains (\" <b>Personal Information</b>\"). We may collect information in a variety of forms and for a variety of purposes (including purposes permitted by applicable law). </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>\n        <b>Collection of Customer Personal Information</b>\n        <p class=\"tnc\">When you create an account on the Platform, or provide your Personal Information through the Platform, the Personal Information that We collect may include, but is not limited to: full name, email address, telephone number, date of birth, gender, identification (including KTP, SIM, passport, or other types of identification), bank account, credit card details, residential address/mailing address and other information required from time to time, in accordance with the needs for Us to be able to provide services, products and/or services to you and in accordance with the Terms of Use required by each type and function of the Platform. In addition, for other information, such as unique identification numbers, e-voucher information, electronic ticket information and/or biometric information that is associated or combined with Personal Information, then such information is also considered Personal Information. The Personal Information that We collect may be provided by You directly or by a third party (for example: when You register or use the Platform, when You contact Our customer service, or otherwise when You provide Personal Information to Us). We may collect information in various forms and purposes (including purposes permitted under applicable laws and regulations). </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <b>Ticket Provider's Collection of Personal Information</b>\n        <p class=\"tnc uk-text-justify\">We will collect Ticket Provider Personal Information when the Ticket Provider registers on Our Platform, collaborates with Us and uses Our Platform, services, products and/or services. The Ticket Provider Personal Information that We will collect includes, but is not limited to: name, email address, telephone number of the Ticket Provider, official name of the business or company registered by the Ticket Provider, corporate documents, Taxpayer Identification Number, and Ticket Provider account data, and all other information and information that We need and will be conveyed to the Ticket Provider from time to time. We will also collect all transaction information, including information on bookings and Ticket purchases that occur on Our Platform after the Ticket Provider is connected to Our Platform. </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <b>Information We collect from you or your mobile device directly</b>\n        <ul class=\"uk-margin-small-top\">\n          <li>When you register and create an account and use the Platform, you must provide Us with certain Personal Information, including your name, physical address, email address, telephone number, and/or a password that you will use to access the Platform after registration. </li>\n          <li>If you are a Customer, when you use the Platform to purchase Tickets, you provide information as relevant, such as, Ticket type, and/or total Ticket transaction cost</li>\n          <li>If you are a Ticket Provider, you will provide Us with order data and data related to Ticket management, the amount of funds for Ticket transactions and/or other data to support the site ecosystem.</li>\n          <li>In connection with payments using electronic money facilities available on Our Platform, We will collect information related to such electronic money transactions by You, including but not limited to the name of the bank, name of the account holder, account number and the amount of funds transacted through such electronic money facilities.</li>\n          <li>If you are a Customer, You can provide a referral code to another party, in the form of a message that We can prepare for You to send or publish via an electronic messaging facility or via a social media provider. You can change the message sentence that We have prepared before You send it. We will not collect data from the party to whom You send the message.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <b>Information collected whenever you use the Platform or visit Our website</b>\n        <ul class=\"uk-margin-small-top\">\n          <li> Each time you use or visit Our Platform, We may collect certain technical data in connection with your use such as, internet protocol address, information on previously or subsequently viewed web pages, duration of each visit/session, internet device identity or media access control address, and information regarding the manufacturer, model, and operating system of the device you use to access Our Platform. </li>\n          <li> When you use or visit Our Platform, certain information may also be collected automatically using cookies. Cookies are small data files stored on your computer or mobile device. We use cookies to track User activity in order to improve the User interface and experience and to remember your browsing preferences within Our Platform. Most mobile devices and internet browsers support the use of cookies; however, you can adjust the settings on your mobile device or internet browser to refuse certain types of cookies or certain specific cookies. Your mobile device and/or browser also allows you to delete any cookies that have previously been stored. However, this may affect the functionality available on Our Platform or website. </li>\n          <li> Whenever you use the Platform via a mobile device, We will track and collect your geographic location information in real time. In some cases, you will be asked or required to activate the Global Positioning System (GPS) on your mobile device to enable Us to provide you with a better experience in using the Platform. You may temporarily disable geographic location tracking information on your mobile device. However, this may affect the functions available on the Platform. </li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <b>Information collected from third parties</b>\n        <p class=\"tnc\">We may also collect your Personal Information from third parties (including affiliates, agents, vendors, suppliers, contractors, partners and others who provide services to Us, perform tasks on Our behalf, or with whom We collaborate). In such cases, We will only collect your Personal Information for or in connection with the purposes for which such third party is involved or the purposes for which We collaborate with such third party (as the case may be).</p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <b>Information about third parties that you provide to Us</b>\n        <p class=\"tnc\">You may provide Us with Personal Information relating to other third party individuals (including Personal Information relating to your spouse, family members, friends or other individuals). You will of course need their prior consent to do so - see <b>\"Acknowledgement and Consent\"</b>, below, for more information. </p>\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Use of Personal Information</b>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"tnc uk-text-justify\">You agree to provide Personal Information to Us and We may use your Personal Information for the following purposes or other purposes permitted by applicable laws and regulations:</p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>If you are a User, We may use your Personal Information: <ul>\n          <li>To identify and register you as a User and to administer, deactivate, or manage your account;</li>\n          <li>To facilitate or enable any verification that We deem necessary before We register you as a User, including the Know Your Customer process;</li>\n          <li>To facilitate the use of services, products, services and/or access to the Platform;</li>\n          <li>To process orders you submit through the Platform to third-party sellers. Payments for products you make through the Platform, whether to third-party sellers, will be processed by Our agents;</li>\n          <li>To deliver products purchased through the Platform, which are sold by third party sellers. We may pass your Personal Information to third parties in order to deliver products to you (for example to our couriers or suppliers), whether the products are sold through the Platform by us or a third party seller;</li>\n          <li>To provide you with product delivery information, whether sold through the Platform by Us or third party sellers, and for consumer support purposes;</li>\n          <li>To compare information, and verify it with third parties in order to ensure the accuracy of the information;</li>\n          <li>To verify and carry out financial transactions in relation to payments you make online; audit the download of data from the Platform; </li>\n          <li>To notify you of any updates to the Platform or changes to the services provided, update the layout and/or content of the Platform pages and customize them for Users;</li>\n          <li>To identify visitors to the Platform and conduct research on the demographics and behavior of Our Users;</li>\n          <li>To maintain, develop, test, improve and personalize the Platform to meet your needs and preferences as a User; </li>\n          <li>To expand and/or improve the products, services and services that We provide, including but not limited to the interface and your experience using Our Platform;</li>\n          <li>To send marketing communications, promotional materials, surveys about Our products and services or third party sellers from time to time or newsletters from Us and Our affiliates and partners;</li>\n          <li>To process and respond to questions and suggestions received from you; and</li>\n          <li>For other uses by us in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li>If you are a Ticket Provider, We may use your Personal Information to: <ul>\n          <li>Identify you and register you as a Ticket Provider, as well as administer, manage, or verify your Account;</li>\n          <li>Facilitate or enable any verification that We, at Our discretion, deem necessary before registering you as a Ticket Provider;</li>\n          <li>Enable you to provide your products to Users;</li>\n          <li>Process, facilitate, and complete payments to you for the products you have provided;</li>\n          <li>Communicate with you and send you information related to the provision of your products, including transmitting User orders to you and facilitating your acceptance of those orders;</li>\n          <li>Provide you with notifications and updates on the Platform or changes in how services, products, and/or offerings are provided;</li>\n          <li>Provide you with reports related to the products you have provided;</li>\n          <li>Process and respond to User feedback regarding the products you have provided;</li>\n          <li>Maintain, develop, test, improve, and personalize the Platform to meet your needs and preferences as a Service Provider;</li>\n          <li>Monitor and analyze activities, behaviors, and demographic data, including the habits and responsiveness of Ticket Providers to various services available on the Platform;</li>\n          <li>Offer or provide services from Our affiliates or partners;</li>\n          <li>Expand and/or improve the products, services, and offerings We provide, including but not limited to interface and user experience;</li>\n          <li>Send you marketing communications, advertisements, promotions, surveys, and special offers or targeted promotions; and</li>\n          <li>Any other use by Us in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li>Whether you are a User or a party providing Personal Information to Us, We may also use your Personal Information more generally for the following purposes (although in certain cases, We will act reasonably and not use your Personal Information beyond what is necessary for these purposes): <ul>\n          <li>To carry out related business processes and functions;</li>\n          <li>To monitor application usage and manage, support, and improve performance efficiency, development, User experience, and Platform functions;</li>\n          <li>To provide assistance in resolving technical difficulties or operational issues with the Platform or services;</li>\n          <li>To generate statistical information and anonymous analytical data for testing, research, analysis, product development, commercial partnerships, and collaborations;</li>\n          <li>To prevent, detect, and investigate any prohibited, illegal, unauthorized, or fraudulent activities;</li>\n          <li>To facilitate business asset transactions (which may include mergers, acquisitions, or asset sales) involving Us and/or Our affiliates; and</li>\n          <li>To enable Us to comply with all obligations under applicable laws and regulations (including but not limited to responding to requests, investigations, or regulatory directives) and conducting audits, due diligence, and investigations.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b> DISCLOSURE OF PERSONAL INFORMATION </b>\n    </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li> We may disclose or share your Personal Information with affiliates and other parties for the following purposes, as well as for other purposes permitted by applicable laws and regulations: <ul>\n          <li>If you are a User, to enable Ticket Providers to provide services to you;</li>\n          <li>If you are a Ticket Provider, to enable Users to receive services from you;</li>\n          <li>For payment processing purposes, We may disclose your Personal Information, such as credit card number, the name on your credit card, or the account number you use for transaction payments through the Platform, to the relevant bank or your credit card issuer;</li>\n          <li>If required or authorized by applicable laws and regulations (including but not limited to responding to inquiries from regulatory bodies or authorities, investigations, or guidelines, or complying with filing and reporting requirements under the law), for purposes specified in applicable regulations;</li>\n          <li>If there is any legal process of any kind between you and Us, or between you and another party, in connection with or related to the services, for the purposes of such legal proceedings;</li>\n          <li>In relation to any verification process that We or the Ticket Provider deem necessary before registering you as a User, including the Know Your Customer (KYC) process;</li>\n          <li>In case of an emergency related to your health and/or safety (whether you are a User or a Ticket Provider) to address the emergency situation;</li>\n          <li>In connection with mergers, corporate asset sales, consolidations, restructurings, financing, or acquisitions of all or part of Our business by or to another company, for the purpose of such transactions (even if the transaction is not ultimately completed);</li>\n          <li>To third parties (including agents, vendors, suppliers, contractors, partners, and other parties providing services to Us or you, performing tasks on Our behalf, or parties with whom We have commercial collaborations), for or in connection with the purposes for which such third parties are engaged or for Our cooperation with such third parties (depending on the circumstances), which may include allowing such third parties to introduce or offer products or services to you, or conducting other activities including marketing, research, analysis, and product development; and</li>\n          <li>In cases where We share Personal Information with affiliates, We do so with the intention that they assist Us in providing the Platform, operating Our business (including, when you subscribe to Our mailing list, for direct marketing purposes), or for data processing purposes on Our behalf. For example, an affiliate of Ours in another country may process and/or store your Personal Information on behalf of Our group company in your country. All Our affiliates are committed to processing the Personal Information they receive from Us in accordance with this Privacy Policy and applicable laws and regulations.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li> When Personal Information no longer needs to be associated with you, We will make reasonable efforts to remove its association with you as an individual before disclosing or sharing such information. </li>\n      <li> We will not sell or rent your Personal Information. </li>\n      <li> In addition to what is set out in this Privacy Policy, We may disclose and share your Personal Information if We have notified you and obtained your consent for such disclosure or sharing. </li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>STORAGE OF PERSONAL INFORMATION</b>\n    </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>Your Personal Information will only be retained for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes of its collection or as long as such retention is required or permitted by applicable laws and regulations. We will cease to retain Personal Information or remove the means by which the Personal Information can be associated with you as an individual as soon as it is deemed that the purpose for collecting the Personal Information is no longer necessary and retention is no longer required for business or legal purposes.</li>\n      <li>Please note that there is still a possibility that some of your Personal Information may be retained by other parties (including by Ticket Providers if you are a User; or by Users if you are a Ticket Provider) in certain ways. Information transmitted through communications between Users and Ticket Providers that occur outside the use of the Platform (such as via phone calls, SMS, mobile messages, or other communication methods) may also be stored in various ways. We do not authorize or encourage the retention of Personal Information in such a manner, and We are not responsible to you for such retention. We shall not be liable for the retention of your Personal Information. You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold Us, Our officers, directors, employees, agents, partners, suppliers, contractors, and affiliates harmless from and against any and all claims, losses, liabilities, costs, damages, and expenses (including but not limited to full legal fees and indemnity costs) arising directly or indirectly from any unauthorized retention of your Personal Information.</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b> ACCESS AND CORRECTION OF PERSONAL INFORMATION </b>\n    </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>Subject to applicable laws and regulations, you may update your Personal Information at any time by accessing your account on the Platform. If you do not have an account with Us, you may contact Us at the email address provided below.</li>\n      <li>We reserve the right to take steps to share updates to your Personal Information with third parties and Our affiliates if your Personal Information is still necessary for the purposes mentioned above.</li>\n      <li>If you wish to view the Personal Information We hold about you or inquire about your Personal Information that has been or may be used or disclosed by Us in the past year, please contact Us at Our email address below. We reserve the right to charge a reasonable administrative fee for this request.</li>\n      <li>If you have a Platform account, you can access your order details by logging into your account on the Platform. Here, you can view your completed order details, pending orders, upcoming shipments, manage your full address details, bank information, and any newsletters you may have subscribed to.</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Where We Store Your Personal Information</b>\n    </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>The Personal Information We collect from you may be stored, transferred, or processed by third-party Ticket Providers. We will use all reasonable efforts to ensure that all such third-party Ticket Providers provide a level of protection comparable to Our commitments under this Privacy Policy.</li>\n      <li>Your Personal Information may also be stored or processed outside of your country by parties working for Us in another country or by third-party Ticket Providers, vendors, suppliers, partners, contractors, or Our affiliates. In such cases, We will ensure that the Personal Information remains subject to a level of protection comparable to that required under your country's laws (and, in any case, in line with Our commitments under this Privacy Policy).</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Security of Personal Information</b>\n    </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>The confidentiality of your Personal Information is of the utmost importance to Us. We will make our best efforts to protect and secure your data and Personal Information from unauthorized access, collection, use, or disclosure, as well as from unlawful processing, accidental loss, destruction, damage, or similar risks. However, transmitting information over the internet is not entirely secure. While We will do Our best to protect your Personal Information, you acknowledge that We cannot guarantee the integrity and accuracy of any Personal Information you transmit over the Internet or ensure that such Personal Information will not be intercepted, accessed, disclosed, altered, or destroyed by unauthorized third parties due to factors beyond Our control. You are responsible for safeguarding your account details, including your username, password, and order details, and must not share them with unauthorized third parties. We are not liable for any misuse of your username, password, and order details except as stated in the respective Terms &amp; Conditions of the Platform. You must also always ensure and take responsibility for the security of the device you use.</li>\n      <li>We ensure that all collected information is securely stored. We protect your Personal Information by: <ul>\n          <li>Restricting access to personal information</li>\n          <li>Keeping up with security technology advancements to prevent unauthorized computer access</li>\n          <li>Securely deleting your Personal Information when it is no longer needed for legal or business purposes</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li>Our Platform uses 256-bit encryption technology and 2048-bit SSL (secure socket layer) when processing your financial details. The encryption technology We use is the industry security standard.</li>\n      <li>Your password is the key to accessing your account. Please use a unique combination of numbers, letters, and special characters, and do not share your account password with anyone. If you share your password with others, you will be responsible for all actions and consequences taken under your account. If you lose control of your password, you may lose control of your Personal Information and other details submitted on the Platform. You may also be subject to legally binding actions taken on your behalf. Therefore, if your password has been compromised for any reason, or if you have reason to believe that it has been compromised, you must immediately contact Us and change your password. You are reminded to always log off from your account and close your browser when using a shared computer.</li>\n      <li>Spam, spyware, or viruses are not allowed on the Platform. Please set and maintain your communication preferences so that We can send communications as per your request. You are not permitted to add other Users (even those who have purchased items from you) to your mailing list (email or physical mail) without their consent. You must not send messages containing spam, spyware, or viruses through the Platform. If you wish to report a suspicious message, please contact Us at Our email address below.</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Changes to the Privacy Policy</b>\n    </p>\n    <p>We may periodically review and modify this Privacy Policy at Our sole discretion from time to time to ensure that it remains consistent with Our future developments and/or changes in legal or regulatory requirements. Any changes to this policy will be published on the Platform or sent via the email address registered in your account. You agree that you are responsible for regularly reviewing this Privacy Policy for the latest information on Our data processing and data protection practices. By continuing to use Our Platform or website, communicating with Us, or accessing and using the services after any changes to this Privacy Policy, you will be deemed to have accepted the Privacy Policy and any revisions thereof.</p>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Acknowledgement and Consent</b>\n    </p>\n    <ol type=\"a\">\n      <li>By agreeing to this Privacy Policy, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and accepted all the terms within it. Specifically, you agree and give consent to Us to collect, use, share, disclose, store, transfer, and/or process your Personal Information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.</li>\n      <li>In cases where you provide Us with Personal Information relating to other individuals (such as Personal Information of your spouse, family members, friends, or other parties), you represent and warrant that you have obtained their consent for, and hereby agree on their behalf to, the collection, use, disclosure, and processing of their Personal Information by Us.</li>\n      <li>You may withdraw your consent for any or all collection, use, or disclosure of your Personal Information at any time by providing Us with reasonable written notice using the contact details provided below. You may also withdraw consent for receiving certain communications and information from Us through the \"opt-out\" or \"unsubscribe\" options available in Our messages to you. Depending on the circumstances and the nature of the consent you withdraw, you must understand and acknowledge that after such withdrawal, you may no longer be able to use the Platform or services. Withdrawal of your consent may result in the termination of your Account or contractual relationship with Us, with all rights and obligations arising therefrom being fully settled. Upon receiving notice of withdrawal of consent for the collection, use, or disclosure of your Personal Information, We will inform you of any possible consequences of the withdrawal so that you can decide whether to proceed with withdrawing your consent.</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"uk-text-justify\">\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Marketing and Promotional Materials</b>\n    </p>\n    <p> You consent to Us and Our affiliates or partners sending you direct marketing, advertisements, and promotional communications via push notifications, messages through the Platform, mail, phone calls, short message service (SMS), and email (\" <b>Marketing Materials</b>\"). You may choose to opt out of receiving such marketing communications at any time by clicking the \"unsubscribe\" option available in the respective message or by contacting Us using the contact details provided below. Please note that if you choose to opt out, We may still send you non-promotional messages, such as receipts or information regarding your Account. </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>ANONYMOUS DATA</b>\n    </p>\n    <p>We may create, use, license, or disclose Personal Information, provided that (i) all identifiable elements have been removed so that the data, whether alone or in combination with other available data, cannot be linked to, associated with, or used to identify any individual, and (ii) similar data has been aggregated so that the original data forms part of a larger dataset.</p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>Third Party Platforms</b>\n    </p>\n    <p>The Platform, website, and Marketing Materials may contain links to websites operated by third parties. We do not control, accept responsibility for, or assume liability for these websites and for the collection, use, maintenance, sharing, or disclosure of data and information by such third parties. Please read the terms and conditions and privacy policies of these third-party websites to understand how they collect and use your Personal Information. <br>\n      <br>Advertisements on our Platform and Marketing Materials serve as links to the advertisers’ websites, and any information they collect based on your click on such links will be collected and used by the relevant advertisers in accordance with their respective privacy policies.\n    </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p class=\"tnc\">\n      <b>How to Contact Us</b>\n    </p>\n    <p></p>\n    <p>If you wish to withdraw your consent for the use of personal information, request access to and/or correction of your Personal Information, have any questions, comments, or concerns, or need assistance regarding technical matters, please do not hesitate to contact us at: <br>\n      <br>\n      <b> PT Global Loket Sejahtera </b>\n      <br> Jl. Empu Sendok No. 30, South Jakarta <br> Email: <a href=\"mailto:support@loket.com\" class=\"ss-link-text\"> support@loket.com </a>\n    </p>\n    <p></p>\n  </li>\n</ul>"
          },
